/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * mErrMsg
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * mErrMsg(m, fmt, ...)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) m (motorVars *)          Motor structure pointer
 * (>) fmt (const char *)       Format for message
 * (>) ... ()                   Additional arguments
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Record error message
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Records an error message relating to motor motion for use by
 * the upper level EPICS code, and logs it via the EPICS/VxWorks
 * LogMessage system.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * sendToMotorDriver
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * sendToMotorDriver(controller, string, response)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) controller (int)     Which controller
 * (>) string (char *)      The motor commands to send
 * (>) response (char *)    Response pointer
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Send command to motor controller
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This is the main interface above the interrupt level to the
 * motor controller hardware.  The specified string is sent to the
 * specified motor controller.  
 *
 * If the response string pointer is null, don't wait for
 * the response.  Otherwise, wait for the response which will be written
 * to the area pointed to by "response".  For commands which don't
 * require a response, use 'noWait' instead of 'waitFor'.
 *
 * Since the motor controller requires that commands be separated by
 * spaces, for safety's sake, all commands should end in a space.
 * Since the commands for one motor cannot be interspersed with
 * anothers, access to the core of this routine is controlled by
 * a semaphore (semOut).
 * 
 * Messages are stored in the outRing ring buffer, and then transmit
 * buffer interrupts are enabled.  This enabling will cause an
 * interrupt (assuming the hardware buffer is empty) and the first character
 * in the ring buffer will be sent.
 *
 * If a response is expected, the code waits on semResponse for a short
 * time (response commands are actived upon by the controller quickly).
 *
 * Finally, once the message is sent (and the response, if any, obtained),
 * the code gives semOut, allowing the next task waiting for this routine
 * to proceed.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 * sendToMotorDebug
 *      0       Print no debugging information
 *      1       Print commands sent to motor
 *      2       Print commands and timeout lengths
 *      3       Print commands, timeouts, and responses.
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * getMdStatus
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * getMdStatus(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor of interest
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Determine motor status
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Query the motor controller for status for this motor, and record that
 * in the status word in the motor structure.  Also note if overtravel
 * has occured (motor is on but isEnabled bit is low) and if the
 * controller fault line is asserted (low).
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * motorTimeout
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * motorTimeout(dist, ms)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) dist (int)           Distance to go
 * (>) ms (motion *)        Pointer to motion parameters
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Calculate minimum timeout
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * From the acceleration, velocity, and distance, calculate the length
 * of time the motion will take.  Return that, in clock ticks, or, if
 * less than a minimum, return the minimum.  Given these parameters,
 * the controller has no ability to vary the length of time it takes to
 * make the motion.  
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
