/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * initMotors
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * initMotors()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Initialize motor software and hardware
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Sets up the semaphore and task used by the VxWorks command line
 * control (doAll) to move motors.  Then resets the Phytron motor
 * driver, and sends an initialization string for this motor to the
 * motor controller.  If this succeeds, reads current position and
 * and current velocity.
 * 
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * motorTask
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * motorTask(motor, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8, a9)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor this task controls
 * (>) a1 (int)             Dummy arguments
 * (>) a2 (int)
 * (>) a3 (int)
 * (>) a4 (int)
 * (>) a5 (int)
 * (>) a6 (int)
 * (>) a7 (int)
 * (>) a8 (int)
 * (>) a9 (int)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Task to move a motor.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * A VxWorks task whose job is to move a particular motor.  This routine
 * is used by the command line diagnosics, and not by the EPICS
 * interface.  The routine it calls, moveOneMotor, is common to both
 * command line and EPICS.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * moveOneMotor
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * moveOneMotor(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Dispatch a motor command
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Used by both command line and by EPICS, this is where the two calling
 * sequences converge.  First off, the position to which the FOCUS motor
 * should be moved may(?) be a function of the positions of all the
 * other mechanisms.  So if a motion command for this mechanism hasn't
 * been commanded, the position for FOCUS is computed.
 *
 * If a motion has been requested, the routine sets EPICS status
 * markers, calls the appropriate routine, and after the routine
 * returns, sets various EPICS status data: is it datumed?  is it parked?
 * health, state, current position.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * noWait
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * noWait(motor, command)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor of interest
 * (>) command (char *)     Command to issue
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Send motor command and return immediately
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Sends a command to the motor (see waitFor) and does not wait for
 * a response or timeout.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * waitFor
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * waitFor(motor, cmdString, wait)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor of interest
 * (>) cmdString (char *)   Command to issue
 * (>) wait (int)           Wait time
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Issue motor command
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Send a command string to the motor.  Wait the given number of
 * clock ticks for interrupt (caused by the 'ID' command).  Then fetch
 * status before returning.
 *
 * An 'ID' is appended to the cmdString and this is passed to the
 * motor controller. If in simulation mode, delay the return if the
 * simulation mode requires an approximation to realistic timing.
 *
 * The main complexity in this routine is handling a timeout error,
 * but overall, it's issue the command, wait on a semaphore longer
 * than we should have to and if the semaphore wait times out, set
 * an error flag.  In any event, set the motor status flags before
 * returning.
 *
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * tellPV
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * tellPV(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor of interest
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Determine position and velocity
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Determines the current position and current velocity of the
 * specified motor.  The velocity is likely to be zero as this routine
 * is most often called after motion has completed.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * motorPos
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * motorPos(motor, where, timeout)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) where (int)          Where to move to
 * (>) timeout (int)        How long to allow (in ticks)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move directly to a given motor position
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * The lowest level of motor command above 'waitFor'.  Moves the
 * motor to the given position.  This is an absolute move if the
 * motor has been datumed, a relative move otherwise.
 *
 * Rotary mechanisms have unbounded motions, which means that the
 * motor controller internal position counter is essentially
 * unbounded while the positions in the configuration file are
 * both bounded and, relatively speaking, small.  This routine
 * has as its primary function the transformation of the unbounded
 * rotary encoder to a bounded "linear" one.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * position
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * position(motor, where)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) where (int)          Where to move
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move motor to a given position
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This is the top level "move" routine.  It does some limit
 * checking and also picks the shortest distance to move for
 * rotary mechanisms. (Note, due to backlash compensation, lower
 * level routines have to worry about this too.)
 *
 * Turns on motor, calls goToPos to do the work, turns off the
 * motor power, and sets status variables.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * goToPos
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * goToPos(motor, where, removeBL)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) where (int)          Where to move
 * (>) removeBL (int)       Remove backlash if true
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move to position, remove backlash 
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This is the workhorse of the upper level positioning routines.
 * The call sequence is
 *    position - goToPos - motorPos - waitFor - sendToMotorDriver
 *
 * Motions in the positive direction are at seek speed until close,
 * then at probe speed until the position is attained.  Motions in
 * the negative direction require backlash removal; they are made
 * at seek speed past the desired position, and then at probe
 * speed until the position is reached.
 *
 * If removeBL is FALSE, act as if there is no backlash to remove.
 *
 * Reaching a limit switch is an error.  Mechanisms which should reach
 * a limit are controlled via findLimit, not position
 *
 * Not useful if motor is not datumed.
 * 
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * checkLimit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * checkLimit(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor of interest
 * (>) flag (int)           What to check for
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns 0, -1, or 1
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Check for limit switch
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * The controller does not report being at a limit if the most
 * recent motion command is in the opposite direction, even if no
 * motion has taken place in that direction.  If flag is POSITIVE or NEGATIVE,
 * set the appropriate motion direction and then check, returning
 * 0 if not at that limit, non-zero otherwise.  If flag
 * is EITHER, don't assert any motion direction, just check the
 * status, returning 1 if at positive limit, -1 if at negative
 * and zero otherwise.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
