 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * motorCreep
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * motorCreep(motor, distance, test)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) distance (int)       Distance to go
 * (>) test (int)           Switch to test
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Creep to a switch position
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Move slowly to a switch position, the point being to measure
 * where the switch activates.  This makes the most sense if distance
 * is positive; assuming the backlash has been removed, the result
 * should be consistent test to test.  If distance is negative,
 * the backlash will interfere!
 *
 * Test is either MH_HOME or MH_LIMIT.  The motion is made one
 * step at a time with the switch status tested each time.
 *
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * motorSteps
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * motorSteps(motor, steps, flag)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) steps (int)          Steps to move
 * (>) flag (int)           Speed to move at
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move motor with relative motion
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Move a specified number of steps.  This is for engineering use.
 * The flag sets the speeds, 0, 1, 2 translating into probe, backOff,
 * and seek rates.
 *
 * There is no backlash compensation; engineers are supposed to know
 * what they are doing.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * probeLimSwitch
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * probeLimSwitch(motor, condition)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) condition (int)      Condition to test for
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move slowly into a limit.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Move toward a limit , and return when at that position.
 * When routine is called, motor should be within a backlash
 * distance, or so, from the desired (real) limit.
 *
 * When probing for a hard limit, the soft limit is checked for first.
 * So if the routine returns successfully, both soft and hard limits
 * in that direction are working properly.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * findTheLimit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * findTheLimit(motor, which)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) which (int)          Limit to check
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Find a limit
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Find a particular switch.
 * Move to a position just shy of switch, then use probe speed
 * to move slowly into switch -- probeLimSwitch().
 *
 * This routine can be called even if the system is not datumed, in which
 * case the limit is approached at high speed and it is likely the
 * hard limit will be triggered (see chargeLimit).
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * chargeLimit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * chargeLimit(motor, s)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) s (switchType *)     Pointer to switch descriptor
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move quickly to a switch
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Go rushing into the soft positive or negative limit,
 * then backoff a bit.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * gotoLimit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * gotoLimit(motor, type)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) limit (int)          Limit to go to
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move to a limit (BINARY only)
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Request motion to a limit; intended for BINARY motors only.  Called
 * only by the valid/moveOneMotor sequence.  This routine allows one
 * to call for positioning to the limit one is already at, and no
 * motion will occur.  Calling findLimit directly will cause the
 * mechanism to back off first, then find the limit.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * findLimit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * findLimit(motor, type)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 * (>) type (int)           Limit to find
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Find a limit (top level call)
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Finds a limit.  Calls findTheLimit to do the real work.  The
 * separation is needed for the datum routine.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * setHome
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * setHome(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to move
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Locate home switch
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This routine finds the home position.  It is not to be called if the home
 * position is at a limit.  Use 'MA', or the 'KR' or 'KM', commands to get
 * close without changing the position counter.  Then backoff, and
 * approach slowly.  This routine is meant to be called only when the
 * motor has not been datumed, since it will reset the home position.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * datum
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * datum(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to datum
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Datum the motor
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Find the home position and set the internal counter to the
 * correct value such that the switch position is at zero.  For
 * home switches, this is done automatically, but we have to fake it
 * for limit switches used as home positions.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * abortMotor
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * abortMotor(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to stop
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Abort motor motion
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Aborts any motion in progress for the specified motor.  Avoiding
 * a race condition is the only real concern here.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * testOMSCards
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * testOMSCards()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Test the OMS cards
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Test to see if OMS VME cards are alive.  This is done by sending
 * a "who are you" ("WHY") message and comparing the response with
 * an expected string.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * motorHealthTree
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * motorHealthTree()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns (encoded) health
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Calculates system health
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Composites the health of the motors into one health for the 
 * mechanism.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * isBusy
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * isBusy(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor in question
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (BOOL) Returns the motor's BUSY status.
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * 
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Determine if motor is BUSY or not.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * isInError
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * isInError(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor in question
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (BOOL) Returns the motor's status inforation
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Returns the motor's ERROR condition.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Returns true if the ERROR flag is set.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
